  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c6fd965debd544d6a9d8c35a992a0ad0",
      "statement": "Invitation acceptance is implemented by a single unguarded `Accept` component registered at two entry paths — `/auth/activate?email=...&token=...` for new users and `/invitations/accept?email=...&token=...` for existing users — only when `environment.features.teamInvitations` is enabled; neither path uses `authGuard` or `publicGuard` so signed-out invitees and people without an account can use it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.routes.ts#L68-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0488b7ae73c6ecd299901b458f1d19859cce3095c16c5a0e5cfa4f7dcffc0d11:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:566b36859a0e790cd774e87a5ce6450c9cc9cf80f7ea593b47ab1eb420cc8a0c"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_62670ecdc1504fe29c180ffa442bab8e",
      "statement": "Because the accept route is unguarded, the `Accept` constructor loads the session itself (`checkSession()` when `getToken()` is truthy) and then fetches the invitation via `auth.getInvitation(email, token)`; a 404 from that fetch while a token is present redirects to `/` so a signed-in user revisiting an already-accepted link (e.g. after a consents-gate reload) lands in the app instead of an invalid-link error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.ts#L21-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:637bbe5e9a2bbd7e862ee15824f8a745380d2f5eea1520be591d25650de22e86:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d7fea6bc9f014d8c9ff467fb1baaaa9a",
      "statement": "Once the invitation loads, acceptance has three branches: `isNewUser` shows a set-password form and calls `auth.activate({ email, token, password })` (account activation and sign-in in one response), `auth.isAuthenticated()` shows a one-click join that calls `auth.acceptInvite(token)`, and otherwise a login form calls `auth.login` then `acceptInvite`; the invite-page branch order is `missingParams` → `loading` → `done` → `invitation`, then `isNewUser` before the signed-in check.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.html#L19-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af40a854f603e6963c9a39e9d71f7ced18060c78c7695dc4387e8813a99c7967:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.ts#L50-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c2acc554ac534186b73a495fd2107226748b5ff54a77ccbc4f1bd652936ba52e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_689fdbfedfc743afb459d92a9e051615",
      "statement": "Invitation-acceptance errors map 404 to \"This invitation is invalid or has expired.\" and 401 to \"Invalid password.\", with other failures falling back to the service message; missing `email`/`token` query params short-circuit to an invalid-link page without an API call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.ts#L21-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a6e26a5e119d2baca32fb18c4552ec36f897d656087729efe7b10a6a9fe786f7:"
